1 | devops | Write PRD proposals for issues 2752 and 2753, which you must read in full first, together with docs/prd/00-INDEX.md, docs/prd/01-conventions.md, docs/prd/02-shells.md, docs/prd/pages/atlas-chat.md and docs/prd/pages/flight-detail-fare.md. THIS IS A DOCS ONLY TASK. Change nothing under apps/ and write no product code, no components and no tests. The deliverable is one PRD-only PR. MARK EVERY NEW OR CHANGED BLOCK AS PROPOSED, pending co-founder sign-off. Never write ACCEPTED, never write signed off, never write approved, and never stamp a co-founder name against anything. A block you wrote and stamped in the same commit was never approved by anyone, and that has happened before in this repo. ITEM ONE, issue 2752, included baggage on the flight result card. The helper already exists at apps/web/lib/flight-baggage.ts and is already used by the flight detail modal and the payment confirmation modal. The result card at apps/web/components/chat/search-result-bubbles.tsx renders no baggage at all. Spec the card surface only. THE LOAD BEARING CONSTRAINT, which you must read in flight-baggage.ts before writing a word of it: a count of zero and an ABSENT count are DIFFERENT FACTS. Zero means the airline stated no allowance and it renders. Absent means the airline stated nothing at all and it must render no part whatsoever, never a default and never a zero. That distinction exists because a Finnair Business Classic fare rendered a zero carry on count in production and told a traveller that a business ticket included no cabin bag. The co-founder request says show the number even if it is zero, and for a STATED zero that is exactly right, but the spec must make unmistakably clear that it does not extend to the unknown case. Record the unknown case as an OPEN QUESTION for co-founder decision, offering the two honest options, which are omitting the icon entirely or rendering an explicit unknown state, and recommend one with your reasoning. Do not decide it yourself and do not let the spec imply it is decided. ITEM TWO, issue 2753, a static route map in the right panel below the already ratified header Your trip is taking shape at docs/prd/pages/atlas-chat.md line 288. Spec a STATIC illustration: origin and destination airport dots, a dotted connecting line, and markers for any intermediate stop. No external map provider, no tile server, no CSP change and no recurring cost, and say so in the spec so nobody reaches for a vendor later. The spec must answer all of these rather than leaving them to the implementer: what renders for a multi city or multi leg trip, what renders before any offer is selected, what renders when the trip contains no flights at all such as a stays only trip, and whether the illustration reflects the selected offer or the search as a whole. Include the loading and empty and error triad exactly as docs/prd/01-conventions.md defines it, and reuse existing ratified copy wherever one fits. Any genuinely new string must be marked PROPOSED and listed together in the PR body so a co-founder can approve the copy in one pass. FOR BOTH ITEMS: follow the existing page structure and section numbering conventions rather than inventing a new shape, and put each item in the correct existing page rather than creating a new page unless the index genuinely calls for one. Run make lint if it covers docs and paste the real exit code captured directly rather than read after a pipe. Open a PR referencing issues 2752 and 2753 with Refs and NO closing keyword, because these issues stay open until the code ships after sign-off. Omit any Co-Authored-By trailer. Do not merge. | docs/prd-baggage-card-and-route-map

2 | frontend-critic | READ-ONLY REVIEW of the wave 1 change on branch docs/prd-baggage-card-and-route-map. You are not a producer: no commits, no push, no gh pr review, no gh pr merge, no labels, no test writing, and no edits to the spec. The harness pushes the branch it checks out, so any commit on a producer ref is a production incident. Permitted writes are a slash tmp worktree only. Record the PR head SHA at start and re-check it at report time, and if it moved report BLOCKED with both SHAs. THE QUESTION THAT MATTERS: would an engineer implementing this spec literally, without asking anyone anything, ship something wrong or something that fabricates data. FIRST and most important, read apps/web/lib/flight-baggage.ts and docs/prd/pages/flight-detail-fare.md section 4.2 yourself, then check the baggage spec against them. A spec that says or merely implies that an unknown allowance renders as zero is a BLOCK, because it would put a supplier statement on the card that no supplier made. Check the exact wording, not the intent: ambiguous phrasing that an implementer could reasonably read as always render a number is just as dangerous as an explicit instruction to do so. Confirm the unknown case is recorded as an open question and is NOT presented as decided. SECOND, verify nothing in the diff is stamped ACCEPTED or approved or signed off, and that no co-founder name appears against any block. Everything must read PROPOSED. Report any violation as a BLOCK regardless of how good the content is. THIRD, confirm the diff is docs only: nothing under apps/, no component, no test, no code. FOURTH, for the route map spec, confirm it commits to a static illustration with no external map provider and no tile server, and that it actually answers the multi leg case, the nothing selected yet case, and the trip with no flights case, rather than deferring them to the implementer. A spec that leaves those open is how three engineers ship three different empty states. FIFTH, confirm every genuinely new string is marked PROPOSED and collected in the PR body, and that existing ratified copy was reused where one already fits rather than a near duplicate being invented. SIXTH, confirm both items landed in the correct existing PRD pages per docs/prd/00-INDEX.md rather than in a new page or the wrong page. Post ONE comment on issue 2340 whose first line reads CRITIC PRD BAGGAGE AND ROUTE MAP, with a verdict of SAFE-TO-MERGE or BLOCK-FIX or BLOCK-ESCALATE, per-finding severity and file and line citations. No vendor names, emails, booking ids or gcloud payloads. | docs/prd-baggage-card-and-route-map
